The command shell uses the scripting language called "Command, Automation,
and Query Language" ("CAQL" for short).

Some possible uses of this (not exhaustive) would be:

* Calculations, including mathematical and scientific calculations

* Automating the operation of other programs

* Querying and manipulating data and files with batch operations

* Creating proxy capabilities

* Starting other programs, including to combine them together and to call
them with different capabilities

* Setting up triggerable conditions

* Combining data, actions, etc

(Other uses are also possible; it is a general-purpose programming language
and can be used to write other programs as well. It would also be possible
to write a program in C and compile it.)


